/// How the project's repository is organized, with its frontends: layout
/// monorepo keeps the app, its frontends (web/<name>, from blueprints such
/// as spa) and the TypeScript client (clients/ts) in one repository, as an
/// npm workspace, so that a change to the model, the API and a screen goes
/// in one commit. task web:install installs every frontend's packages,
/// task dev runs the API and the frontends together, task web:build
/// builds them.
blueprint workspace {
  version "0.1.0"
  requires app
  optional client_ts, http, docker, github_actions

  /// monorepo: everything in one repository. (polyrepo, each frontend in a
  /// repository of its own, is planned.)
  option layout name default(monorepo)

  hook post-gen "ignore" edits [".gitignore"]
}
